# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Saga final-chapter exile-return transform (scope §2c, layer L3). Ch III
#   fires on the 3rd lore counter → exile saga → return saga transformed with back-face
#   grpId under our control. Two ObjectIdChanged + two ZoneTransfer (Exile, Return) in
#   one GSM tick, plus grpId swap 79552 → 79553.
# Forcing: saga pre-seeded on BF with 2 lore counters. Only engine action before Ch III
#   is turn-2 draw-step auto-increment (counter → 3 → trigger). No combat, no AI cards,
#   no player choices. The transform is the ONLY interesting event in the puzzle.
# AI behavior: zero AI interaction. Empty board, empty hand. Passes turn 1 automatically.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN (Survive, turn 3 upkeep)  = transform fired + all annotations match (see test asserts)
#   LOSE (turn limit, no xform)    = draw-step auto-increment broken (L4) OR Ch III trigger
#                                     didn't fire (Forge bug — report, don't fix in this PR)
#   WIN but test asserts fail      = transform fired but leyline wire-shape wrong (L3 gap — main target)
#   TIMEOUT                        = SubAbility-chain stall in bridge/StateMapper on
#                                     double ZoneTransfer within one GSM
#   CRASH                          = card/back-face missing, or detector NPE on double-hop
# Card roles:
#   Tribute to Horobi — the subject. Pre-seeded with 2 lore counters to skip Ch I/II.
#   Swamp (humanlibrary) — draw-step fuel for turn 2 (triggers the lore counter auto-add).
#   Swamp (ailibrary) — draw-step fuel for AI turn 1 (prevents AI drawing from empty).
# Protocol path: MechanicAnnotations (CounterAdded emit) → StateMapper.stackAbilityAppearances
#   (Ch III AbilityInstanceCreated) → ChangeZone(Exile) → SubAbility ChangeZone(Return,
#   Transformed=True, GainControl=True) → TransferAnnotations pair for both transfers →
#   ObjectMapper.resolveGrpId picks back-face 79553. Catalog: saga=missing. This is the
#   acceptance test for #191 saga-transform scope / scope-doc §3 L3.
# Asserted by: matchdoor/src/test/kotlin/leyline/game/SagaTransformPuzzleTest.kt —
#   2x ObjectIdChanged + ZT(Exile)+ZT(Return) in one GSM, grpId 79552→79553,
#   othersideGrpId 79552, cardTypes include Creature (back-face Spirit).

[metadata]
Name:Saga Transform — Tribute to Horobi
Goal:Survive
Turns:2
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Pre-seeded 2 lore counters on Tribute to Horobi. Draw step turn 2 triggers Ch III exile-return transform. Tests the two-ObjectIdChanged + ZT(Exile)+ZT(Return) sequence and back-face grpId resolution.

[state]
ActivePlayer=Human
ActivePhase=Main1
HumanLife=20
AILife=20

humanbattlefield=Tribute to Horobi|Counters:LORE=2
humanlibrary=Swamp
ailibrary=Swamp
